      "detail": "every labelled simple graph on 2 to 5 vertices, every missing edge added once: 1606 additions join two components and 3719 do not. On all 1606 of the first kind the difference phi(j) - phi(i) is not fixed by any nearest potential before the action, is fixed after it at exactly the new edge's term, rho^2 does not move, b1 holds and the component count falls by one. On all 3719 of the second kind the difference was already fixed before, b1 rises by one and the component count holds. Compared below 1e-09",
