      "detail": "600 random weighted connected graphs on 8, 16, 32 vertices, a missing edge with a random weight and term added to each. The three closed forms and the new edge's residual D / (1 + w_e R) agree with the numerical projection on every graph, below 1e-09, and the same action with D set to zero moves nothing, also below 1e-09. The fraction of the discrepancy absorbed into the ends' relative level runs from 0.018 to 0.958 across these graphs",
      "kind": "own_reading",
      "name": "B103-2",
      "passed": true,
      "statement": "joining two positions that could reach each other: rho^2 rises by w_e D^2 / (1 + w_e R), every potential moves by w_e D L^+ b / (1 + w_e R), and the ends' relative level moves by the fraction w_e R / (1 + w_e R) of D"
    },
    {
      "detail": "two six-vertex blocks joined by one edge whose conductance walks down 1e+00, 1e-01, 1e-02, 1e-03, 1e-04, and an action joining the far ends. R rises from 2.703 to 10001.7; the fraction of D absorbed into the ends' relative level, measured from the two fits, rises from 0.7299 to 0.999900; the rise in rho^2 and the new edge's residual fall toward zero; D itself does not move; and with the joining edge removed the level is pinned exactly. At the other end, a complete graph on eight vertices less the joined pair, weights walked up 1e+00, 1e+01, 1e+02, 1e+04: the measured fraction falls from 0.2500 to 3.33e-05 and the ends' relative level moves less at every step. On every rung of both walks the measured fraction is w_e R / (1 + w_e R), compared below 1e-09. Checks: the same action with D set to zero moves nothing at any rung: yes; D does not depend on the bridge's conductance: yes; R rises as the bridge weakens: yes; the measured fraction of D absorbed rises toward one: yes; the measured fraction is w_e R / (1 + w_e R) on every rung of both walks: yes; rho^2's increase falls toward zero: yes; the new edge's residual falls toward zero: yes; with the bridge removed the level is pinned exactly: yes; the measured fraction falls toward zero as the ends are tied tighter: yes; the ends' relative level moves less and less: yes",
      "kind": "own_reading",
