    {
      "detail": "B84-4's 10 tableaux redrawn from B81's generator with seed 84 + 3; the same edges come back (yes). With R computed from each tableau, not fitted, the closed form matches the recorded distance on every rung below 1e-12. The printed low end 0.848983 is the rate on step 1 of 4, informative, and equals (1 + w_b R)/(1 + w_a R) there to its noise; the printed high end 1.002530 is the rate on step 4, where the closed form bends by less than the float noise of the distances it divides, so the rate carries nothing. So B84's reading that the approach is linear holds as the weight goes to zero, and the spread it printed is the curvature (1 + w_b R)/(1 + w_a R) at the top of the ladder and noise at the bottom",
